const fq=[['Can you build muscle with calisthenics?','Yes. Muscle grows from hard sets close to failure with rising tension over time. Bodyweight moves do that well as long as you keep moving to harder versions or adding weight.'],['How many sets and reps build muscle with bodyweight?','About 3–4 sets of 6–15 reps per move, ending each set 1–3 reps short of failure, and roughly 10–20 hard sets per muscle group each week.'],['How long does it take to see muscle from calisthenics?','Beginners usually notice changes in 6–12 weeks of consistent training with enough protein. Visible size takes several months.'],['Can calisthenics build big legs?','Yes, with single-leg moves like Bulgarian split squats, shrimp squats and pistols, and by adding load once reps get high. Plain bodyweight squats stop working quickly.'],['Is calisthenics or weights better for muscle?','Both build muscle when sets are hard enough. Weights make loading easier to measure; calisthenics builds strength and skills at the same time with almost no equipment.']];
